# Dissertation core rules

- **Cite Norman et al. 2024** (doi:10.1002/sim.10152) for the base deepAFT formula. R reference: `dnn::deepAFT`.
- **Contribution** = Python package + limitation-aware extensions + **simulation** + **TCGA** glioma survival (GDC + genes) + **BraTS 2024 GLI** imaging/multimodal pipeline (dissertation scope—all three results areas).
- **Never** add C-index or benchmark numbers to README unless from a completed run in `results/`.
- **BraTS 2024 GLI** has segmentation MRI; OS for linked multimodal rows comes from **GDC/TCGA** when a mapping file exists (official 2024↔TCGA table not in public challenge materials checked here—document source when reporting linked results).
- **OncoLnc** expression OK; use **GDC** for vital status (2016 freeze unreliable for GBM).
- Read [AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md) and [PROJECT_TASKS.md](../PROJECT_TASKS.md) for subagent/skill/hook links.
